# What never gets uploaded to a deployment.
#
# Without this file the CLI walks the whole working directory, and this repo
# keeps 15GB of story masters in stories/ — a `vercel deploy` that includes
# them does not finish.
#
# The second reason matters more than the first. Anything uploaded here is
# served from the deployment; anything under public/ ends up at a permanent,
# ungated URL. Premium media must reach a viewer ONLY through the gated routes
# (/api/stream, /api/still), which mint short-lived signed URLs from private
# Vercel Blob after the entitlement check. So the private source folders below
# are excluded on purpose, not merely for size.
#
# Keep this in step with .gitignore: a path that is gitignored but NOT listed
# here still ships, because the CLI uploads the working directory, not HEAD.

# Story video — masters and streaming proxies. Production reads these from
# private Blob (scripts/upload-media.mjs); see lib/media/storage.ts.
stories

# Members-only stills, and the raw source they are cut from. Same private-Blob
# model as the video above. public/gallery/** (the free card covers) still
# ships — that is the only still imagery meant to be public.
stills-private
stills
stills-src
public/stills

# Large room-capture binaries, hosted out of band.
public/scans
public/panos
public/splats

# Build output — Vercel builds from source.
.next

# Local env and tooling.
.env*.local
.git
